      "text": "Diels–Alder: cyclopentadiene + maleic anhydride\n\nA concerted [4+2] cycloaddition giving the endo adduct: six electrons move in one cyclic transition state.\n\nDiels–Alder: cyclopentadiene + maleic anhydride: 2 reactant(s) → 1 product(s), 2 states.\nStates: Reactants → Endo adduct.\nOverall ΔH = -150 kJ/mol; highest transition state 55 kJ/mol above the reactants (the rate-determining step is Reactants → Endo adduct).\nOne barrier (55 kJ/mol) and a strongly exothermic step (−150 kJ/mol): the reaction is fast at room temperature.",
